oral Gables.","facts":["Built in 1925 as the office of architect H. George Fink, a cousin of founder George Merrick.","Many early Coral Gables homes were designed here starting in 1925.","Address: 2506 Ponce de Leon Boulevard, Coral Gables"],"images":[],"free":null,"bookingUrl":null,"typicalMinutes":30,"source":"osm","osmUrl":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/14099749569","factSources":{"Built in 1925 as the office of architect H. George Fink, a cousin of founder George Merrick.":"https://www.loc.gov/item/fl0870/","Many early Coral Gables homes were designed here starting in 1925.":"https://coralgablesmagazine.com/historic-preservation/"}},{"id":"osm-n5679960544","popularity":1,"name":"Iron Arrow Mound","region":"miami","lat":25.720382,"lng":-80.277914,"categories":["history-culture"],"topic":"monument","summary":"Monument.","facts":["Iron Arrow was founded in November 1926 by first University of Miami president Bowman Foster Ashe.","The society is based on the ideals and traditions of the Seminole Indian Nation.","Inductees keep a 24-hour drum vigil and tend fires on the mound.","Inscription: “IA Iron Arrow Honor Society Insignia FOUNDED IN 1926 AS THE UNIVERSITY'S HIGHEST HONOR \"HE WHO WOULD KNOW THE ARROW MUST AS AN IRREFUTABLE RULE HAVE OPENLY AND WITHOUT THOUGHT OF REWARD SHOWN OBVIOUS LOVE OF ALMA MATER”"],"images":[],"free":null,"bookingUrl":null,"typicalMinutes":30,"source":"osm","osmUrl":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/5679960544","factSources":{"Iron Arrow was founded in November 1926 by first University of Miami president Bowman Foster Ashe.":"https://news.miami.edu/com/stories/2013/09/iron-arrow.html","The society is based on the ideals and traditions of the Seminole Indian Nation.":"https://news.miami.edu/com/stories/2013/09/iron-arrow.html","Inductees keep a 24-hour drum vigil and tend fires on the mound.":"https://news.miami.edu/com/stories/2013/09/iron-arrow.html"}},{"id":"osm-n1577578109","popularity":1,"name":"Jose Marti Memorial","region":"miami","lat":25.764408,"lng":-80.216429,"categories":["history-culture"],"topic":"monument","summary":"Monument.","facts":["A plaque marks the 100th anniversary of Jose Marti's death in 1995, donated by the Knights of Columbus.","The park also has a map of Cuba with a quote from Marti."],"images":[],"free":null,"bookingUrl":null,"typicalMinutes":30,"source":"osm","osmUrl":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/1577578109","factSources":{"A plaque marks the 100th anniversary of Jose Marti's death in 1995, donated by the Knights of Columbus.":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g34438-d19101234-Reviews-Cuban_Memorial_Boulevard_Park-Miami_Florida.html","The park also has a map of Cuba with a quote from Marti.":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g34438-d19101234-Reviews-Cuban_Memorial_Boulevard_Park-Miami_Florida.html"}},{"id":"osm-n6583012889","popularity":1,"name":"Julia B. Tuttle's Homestead","region":"miami","lat":25.770915,"lng":-80.19232,"categories":["history-culture"],"topic":"historic site","summary":"Historic site.","facts":["Tuttle bought 644 acres on the north bank of the Miami River, including Fort Dallas.","Her home was a two-story stone building, built in 1849 as Fort Dallas officers' quarters.","A marker for Tuttle was erected in 2020 by Miami-Dade County at Fort Dallas Park."],"images":[],"free":null,"bookingUrl":null,"typicalMinutes":45,"source":"osm","osmUrl":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/6583012889","factSources":{"Tuttle bought 644 acres on the north bank of the Miami River, including Fort Dallas.":"https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=250418","Her home was a two-story stone building, built in 1849 as Fort Dallas officers' quarters.":"https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=250418","A marker for Tuttle was erected in 2020 by Miami-Dade County at Fort Dallas Park.":"https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=250418"}},{"id":"osm-n6594610104","popularity":1,"name":"Julia Deforest Tuttle","region":"miami","lat":25.793427,"lng":-80.191689,"categories":["history-culture"],"topic":"memorial","summary":"Memorial.","facts":["Julia Tuttle is buried in the Miami City Cemetery.","Tuttle is the only woman to found a major U.S. city."],"images":[],"free":null,"bookingUrl":null,"typicalMinutes":30,"source":"osm","osmUrl":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/6594610104","factSources":{"Julia Tuttle is buried in the Miami City Cemetery.":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miami_City_Cemetery","Tuttle is the only woman to found a major U.S. city.":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julia_Tuttle"}},{"id":"osm-n6583009086","popularity":1,"name":"Julia Sturtevant Tuttle","region":"miami","lat":25.773447,"lng":-80.185601,"categories":["history-culture"],"topic":"statue","summary":"Statue.","facts":["The 10-foot bronze statue shows Tuttle holding oranges and blossoms.","Scenes from Miami's 1896 incorporation are engraved on the statue's skirt.","Unveiled July 28, 2010, by the Miami-Dade County Commission for Women and partners."],"images":[],"free":null,"bookingUrl":null,"typicalMinutes":30,"source":"osm","osmUrl":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/6583009086","factSources":{"The 10-foot bronze statue shows Tuttle holding oranges and blossoms.":"https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/26464","Scenes from Miami's 1896 incorporation are engraved on the statue's skirt.":"https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/26464","Unveiled July 28, 2010, by the Miami-Dade County Commission for Women and partners.":"https://www.facebook.com/MiamiDadeWomen/photos/statue-of-julia-s-tuttle-miamis-founding-mother-at-bayfront-park-in-downtown-mia/10151348375859142/"}},{"id":"osm-w120105957","popularity":3,"name":"Lincoln Theatre","region":"miami","lat":25.790888,"lng":-80.134016,"categories":["history-culture"],"topic":"historic site","summary":"Historic site.","facts":["Designed by Thomas W. Lamb with local architect Robert E. Collins.","Operated as a cinema until the 1980s.","The New World Symphony bought it in 1990 and performed there until 2011.","Founded in 1936","Design